*  THE FOUR WITNESS SHAPES of queue row `subscript-silent-accept`, one statement each,
*  every one with a PLAIN UNSET VARIABLE as the subscripted operand (SPITBOL: the null
*  string) -- rvalue, multi-subscript, nested, and ASSIGNMENT TARGET.  The lvalue shape
*  is here on its own line because an assignment target takes a different road through
*  the lowerer (sx_subscript_lv, not the TT_IDX rvalue arm) and a cure that only fixes
*  reads would leave it silently accepting.  Every line is Appendix D 235; &ERRLIMIT
*  converts so the codes are pinnable.  The array/table tails are the POSITIVE CONTROL
*  in the SAME shapes, so a cure that made every subscript error cannot pass this file.
        &ERRLIMIT = 100
        X = A[1]                                :F(F1)
        OUTPUT = 'rvalue       accepted'        :(N1)
F1      OUTPUT = 'rvalue       ' &ERRTYPE
N1      X = B[1, 2]                             :F(F2)
        OUTPUT = 'multi        accepted'        :(N2)
F2      OUTPUT = 'multi        ' &ERRTYPE
N2      X = C[D[1]]                             :F(F3)
        OUTPUT = 'nested       accepted'        :(N3)
F3      OUTPUT = 'nested       ' &ERRTYPE
N3      E[1] = 'hello'                          :F(F4)
        OUTPUT = 'lvalue       accepted'        :(N4)
F4      OUTPUT = 'lvalue       ' &ERRTYPE
N4      G = ARRAY(3)
        G[1] = 'one'
        OUTPUT = 'ok-rvalue    ' G[1]
        H = ARRAY('2,3')
        H[2, 3] = 'two-three'
        OUTPUT = 'ok-multi     ' H[2, 3]
        K = ARRAY(3)
        K[1] = 2
        OUTPUT = 'ok-nested    ' G[K[1] - 1]
        OUTPUT = 'end'
END
